Test Case: disk_os_storage_account_type
================================================================================

Initial Error:
Error: Attempt to get attribute from null value

  on azapi.tf line 51, in resource "azapi_resource" "this":
  51:       type         = identity.value.type
    ├────────────────
    │ identity.value is null

This value is null, so it does not have any attributes.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The dynamic identity block is iterating over a list that contains null when identity is not configured. The can() function on line 49 is checking if the identity attribute exists, but when it exists and is null, the list becomes [null] instead of being empty.
- Fix Method: Change the for_each condition to explicitly check for null and only create the block when identity is not null
- Changes Made: Updated line 49 from `for_each = can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) ? [module.replicator.azapi_header.identity] : []` to `for_each = try(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity, null) != null ? [module.replicator.azapi_header.identity] : []`
- Result: Success - terraform plan now works. Detected drift, analyzing against acceptable_drift_patterns.md

